    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but i've seen a lot of talk lately saying that these programs are actually kind of a distraction or even counterproductive to actual meritocracy. some people say they just create more friction without any real proof of ROI. what's the actual counter-argument to that? like, is there any real data that shows these programs don't just hurt performance?",
